Every app wraps its tree once in `MeowProvider`. It supplies the theme and
manages light/dark mode (following the OS by default), and includes the portal
host that overlays render through.

<Steps>

1. Wrap your root component in `MeowProvider`.
2. Compose screens from components — no per-screen setup.
3. Optionally register an icon renderer.

</Steps>

```tsx
import { MeowProvider, Button, Card, Text, TextInput } from 'react-native-meowui';

export default function App() {
  return (
    <MeowProvider>
      <SignIn />
    </MeowProvider>
  );
}

function SignIn() {
  return (
    <Card outlined style={{ padding: 16, gap: 12 }}>
      <Text variant="headline">Sign in</Text>
      <TextInput label="Email" placeholder="you@example.com" />
      <TextInput label="Password" secureTextEntry />
      <Button fullWidth>
        Continue
      </Button>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

## Dark mode

`MeowProvider` follows the OS color scheme by default. Force a mode, or switch
it at runtime:

```tsx
// Follow the OS (default)
<MeowProvider>{children}</MeowProvider>

// Force a mode
<MeowProvider mode="dark">{children}</MeowProvider>

// Toggle at runtime
function ThemeToggle() {
  const { mode, toggleMode } = useThemeController();
  return (
    <Button variant="ghost" onPress={toggleMode}>
      {mode === 'dark' ? 'Light' : 'Dark'} mode
    </Button>
  );
}
```

Read more in [Dark mode](/theming/dark-mode/).

## Access the theme anywhere

```tsx
import { useTheme } from 'react-native-meowui';

function BrandMark() {
  const { colors, spacing, radii } = useTheme();
  return (
    <View style={{
      backgroundColor: colors.primaryMuted,
      padding: spacing[2],
      borderRadius: radii.sm,
    }}>
      <Text style={{ color: colors.onPrimaryMuted }}>Aa</Text>
    </View>
  );
}
```

`useTheme()` is safe outside a provider — it falls back to the reference light
theme, so components render correctly in isolation (tests, Storybook).

There are three levels of customization, from lightest to heaviest.

## 1. Inline overrides

Pass partial token overrides to `MeowProvider`. They are deep-merged onto the
reference palette for the active mode:

```tsx
import { MeowProvider } from 'react-native-meowui';

<MeowProvider
  overrides={{
    colors: { primary: '#2F6B4F', onPrimary: '#FFFFFF' },
    radii: { md: 9, lg: 14 },
    typography: { body: { fontSize: 16, lineHeight: 23 } },
    metrics: { control: { md: 44 } },
  }}
>
  {children}
</MeowProvider>
```

Override only what you need — everything else stays tuned. Colors override the
**active mode's** palette, so light and dark keep their own values.

## 2. Fonts

Map your font families by weight. `Text` resolves each variant's weight to the
matching family (400 → `regular`, 500 → `medium`, 600 → `semibold`):

```tsx
<MeowProvider
  overrides={{
    fonts: {
      regular: 'Inter-Regular',
      medium: 'Inter-Medium',
      semibold: 'Inter-SemiBold',
    },
  }}
>
  {children}
</MeowProvider>
```

Load the fonts with your usual mechanism (`expo-font`, `react-native.config.js`)
before the provider mounts.

## 3. A fully custom theme

`createTheme` builds a standalone, frozen theme object — useful when the theme
comes from remote config, Redux, or your own design system:

```tsx
import { createTheme, MeowProvider } from 'react-native-meowui';

const brand = createTheme({
  mode: 'dark',
  colors: {
    primary: '#C9A227',
    onPrimary: '#1A1608',
    primaryMuted: '#332B0E',
    onPrimaryMuted: '#E8D68A',
  },
  radii: { sm: 4, md: 8, lg: 12 },
});

<MeowProvider theme={brand}>{children}</MeowProvider>
```

Passing a complete `theme` puts the provider in **controlled mode** — it renders
exactly the theme you gave it and stops resolving modes internally. Combine
with [Dark mode](/theming/dark-mode/#controlled) if you manage the scheme
yourself.

## Deriving tokens is your job

MeowUI includes no color-manipulation library (that would be a runtime
dependency). If your brand needs derived shades — hovers, disabled fills —
precompute them and set the tokens explicitly:

```tsx
const accent = '#2F6B4F';
const theme = createTheme({
  colors: {
    primary: accent,
    primaryMuted: '#E4EFE9',
    onPrimaryMuted: '#1E4A36',
  },
});
```
